From: mscharged-port
Subject: Keep rewound GL resource-pool storage for original writers
Upstream-base: f75ccf1ad20e5bd7585962990db08067c0ae498a
Classification: native ownership contract (shared graphics-storage tracker); depends on 0213 and 0238.

GLXResourcePool::ReleaseResource only moves the pool top on the Wii; the
memory stays valid until the pool allocates over it. Original
DrawableNetMesh::Render relies on that: GameRenderTask resets the net pools
once per frame and renders twice with a secondary NIS (picture-in-picture,
replays), and the second pass allocates its MeshWriter buffers, rewinds the
same pool to its marker, then fills, publishes and draws those buffers.

The native rewind hook now commits through CommitRewind. Completed bytes and
unfinished producers in the range are retired as before, but each graphics
storage record stays (same incarnation) until a later allocation from the pool
evicts it or its backing is freed. Frame-memory retirement still ends storage
lifetime. Pool, marker and renderer code are unchanged.

diff --git a/src/NL/glx/glxMemory.cpp b/src/NL/glx/glxMemory.cpp
--- a/src/NL/glx/glxMemory.cpp
+++ b/src/NL/glx/glxMemory.cpp
@@ -395,8 +395,10 @@
 #if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE) && defined(MSCHARGED_GAME_MODULE)
     mscharged::platform::RetireGameResourceRecords(this,
         (void*)(mPoolMemory[0] + mUsedMemory[0]), mPoolSizes[0] - mUsedMemory[0]);
+    // A rewind only moves the pool top; retail writers may still fill and draw
+    // storage allocated before it (DrawableNetMesh's second pass per frame).
     for (int pool = 0; pool < 2; ++pool)
-        nativeRetirement[pool].Commit((void*)(mPoolMemory[pool] + mUsedMemory[pool]),
+        nativeRetirement[pool].CommitRewind((void*)(mPoolMemory[pool] + mUsedMemory[pool]),
             mPoolSizes[pool] - mUsedMemory[pool]);
 #endif
 #endif
